      "source": "https://westmcleanmcleanneighborhood.org/west-mclean-tracing-the-roots-and-rich-heritage-of-a-community-gem/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community’s name honors John Roll McLean, former publisher of The Washington Post, who helped found the town in 1910 when Lewinsville and Langley merged.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McLean%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "West McLean’s streets are lined with heritage trees and historic landmarks, a legacy championed by local leaders and the McLean Historical Society.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://westmcleanmcleanneighborhood.org/west-mclean-tracing-the-roots-and-rich-heritage-of-a-community-gem/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "McLean Central Park, an 18‑acre green heart just southeast of West McLean, hosts festivals and the annual McLean Day, a tradition lasting over a century.",
